init (6) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * init makes the kernel's kext port, HOST_KEXTD_PORT, for kextd to check
    in as com.blueberrypieos.kextd.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:58:54 +0000

init (5) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * Build-Depend on pietoolchain-host and pietoolchain-sdk.
  * A ZFS root is remounted read-write unless its readonly property is on.
  * init runs /usr/libexec/pie-root-setup, if it is installed, before
    /etc/rc and again once /etc/rc exits.
  * A soft reboot, reboot3() with RB2_USERREBOOT, restarts user space: init
    stops every process, unmounts every file system but the root and /dev,
    switches the root to the ZFS dataset named in /var/run/pie-softreboot
    with pivot_root(2), and runs itself again. It reboots instead if a
    process outlives SIGKILL or a step fails. A failed pie-root-setup makes
    the boot count as failed.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:15:26 +0000

init (3) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * Before a reboot or halt, init runs /etc/rc.shutdown, for 30 seconds at
    most, while it still serves the bootstrap port.
  * The first reboot or halt request decides which one happens.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:16:19 +0000

init (2) blueberry-pie-os; urgency=medium

  * Start getty on the console in place of a root shell.
  * Only root may check in or register a system service name.
  * Bootstrap requests need a send-once reply port and a send right.
  * A console that fails to start is tried again a second later.
  * init makes the port of com.apple.auditd at boot and sets it as the
    host's audit control port. auditd checks it in. Only root may check it in,
    and no one may look it up.

 -- Maxwell <maxwell@blueberrypieos.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:28:13 +0000

